  "$schema": "https://design-tokens.org/schema.json",
  "meta": {
    "name": "Green & Ochre",
    "version": "1.4.0",
    "purpose": "Portfolio + LMS for a software engineer and trainer",
    "note": "Primitives are raw values. Never reference primitives in components — reference semantic tokens only, so rebrands touch one layer.",
    "changelog": [
      "1.1.0 — added semantic.action group and theme.dark, both of which existed in tokens.css but not here; added lmsState.overdue.rail; documented the enrolled/active naming rule.",
      "1.2.0 — tokens.css caught up: it now carries --state-overdue-rail in both themes, closing a drift that had stood since 1.1.0. Named the component layer 'elements' so 'primitive' means one thing. Named the payment component PaymentRail and retired stepper/step/node/connector.",
      "1.3.0 — typography.family.mono is Source Code Pro, replacing JetBrains Mono, which has no U+20A6 naira glyph in any release. The mono unicode-range had declared U+20A6 all along, so every amount set in mono drew its currency symbol from a fallback font. Mono carries the numbers and the numbers are money. Source Code Pro is OFL, variable 400-600, and subsets to 22.1KB against the 31.5KB it replaces.",
      "1.4.0 — added a semantic shape and elevation layer: semantic.surface.radius/radiusSm/radiusLg, semantic.control.radius, semantic.pill.radius, semantic.elevation.raised/floating/overlay. The primitive guard bans --radius-* and --shadow-* in components and nothing sat above them, so a Button had no legal way to round a corner. Spacing and type needed no such layer because --space-5 already names its step; --radius-md does not name 'a card's corner', and both radius and elevation change in a rebrand. The elevation aliases need no dark-mode override — the shadow primitives are already redefined in theme.dark."
    ]
  },
