  "rules": [
    "One ochre element per screen region. Ochre marks the single next action, nothing else.",
    "Green is the workhorse: navigation, links, primary buttons, inverse sections. It also carries the done state — green means progress, consistently.",
    "Mono is reserved for things that are literally code or literally a number.",
    "Every LMS item is exactly one of: locked, active, done, overdue. No fifth state.",
    "The stepped rail is the only decorative motif. Do not add a second.",
    "The visual state 'active' is not the enrollment status. In the database an enrolled learner is 'enrolled'. Enrollment statuses: pending, enrolled, suspended, completed, expired, deferred.",
    "Fonts are self-hosted and Latin-subset with font-display: swap. The unicode-range must include U+20A6 for the naira sign.",
    "'Primitive' means a raw token value and nothing else. The shared component layer — Button, Input, Card, Badge, Rail — is called 'elements'. Folders: components/elements/ for those, then by feature above them.",
    "The payment schedule component is PaymentRail. Its parts are the rail and its knots. 'Stepper', 'step', 'node' and 'connector' are retired from this project.",
    "Instalment vocabulary splits in two. The database column stores unpaid, paid or cancelled. The visual state is done, active, locked or overdue. The mapping is server-derived, never computed in a component.",
    "A class session's visual state comes from entitlement and schedule, never from watch progress. A paid future class session that is not next up carries no badge at all — that is the absence of a state, not a fifth one."
  ],
